{"content_hash": "dbc46835177e71f9", "version_id": 156, "article_id": 16, "level_code": "ja_n5", "lang": "ja", "level": 1, "level_label": "N5 初級", "title": "AIでアドビのソフトを作った人がいる", "title_zh": "有人用AI做了个免费的“Adobe全家桶”", "topic": "tech", "source": "arstechnica", "source_url": "https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/10/software-is-over-bold-ai-developer-takes-aim-at-adobe-with-open-source-clones/", "image": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(343, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(21, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "2a1fc9572154"}, "published_date": "2026-10-07", "word_count": 303, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "ある人がAIを使って、アドビのソフトとよく似たものを作りました。無料で使えます。まだ完成していません。", "lead_zh": "有人用AI做出了和Adobe软件非常相似的东西。免费使用。但还没完成。", "preview": "アメリカにブランドン・トーマスという人がいます。かれはソフトを作る人です。アドビのソフトが高いです。それに、やめるときお金がかかります。かれはそれがいやでした。", "preview_zh": "美国有个叫布兰登·托马斯的人。他是做软件的。Adobe的软件很贵。而且取消订阅还要花钱。他很讨厌这一点。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 146, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/audio/16/ja_n5.mp3", "duration": 63.562, "size_bytes": 385056, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 183, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/data/versions/156.json", "paragraphs": ["アメリカにブランドン・トーマスという人がいます。かれはソフトを作る人です。アドビのソフトが高いです。それに、やめるときお金がかかります。かれはそれがいやでした。", "そこで、AIを使って新しいソフトを作りました。フォトショップやイラストレーターなど、七つのソフトです。見た目も使い方もアドビとよく似ています。ぜひむりょうで使えます。", "トーマスさんは「一か月で百パーセント同じになる」と言いました。でも、あとで「九十九パーセントは、何か月もかかる」と言いました。まだとても早いです。", "このソフトはまだ未完成です。こわれやすいです。それに、アドビとそっくりなので、もんだいになるかもしれません。", "トーマスさんは言います。「ソフトはもうおわりだ。みんなでインターネットをとりもどそう」と。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["美国有个叫布兰登·托马斯的人。他是做软件的。Adobe的软件很贵。而且取消订阅还要花钱。他很讨厌这一点。", "于是他用AI做了新软件。有Photoshop、Illustrator等七款。外观和用法都和Adobe很像。而且完全免费。", "托马斯说“一个月就能做到100%一样”。但后来说“99%得好几个月”。现在还非常早。", "这个软件还没完成。容易出问题。而且和Adobe太像，可能会有法律麻烦。", "托马斯说：“软件已经结束了。大家一起把互联网拿回来。”"], "body": "アメリカにブランドン・トーマスという人がいます。かれはソフトを作る人です。アドビのソフトが高いです。それに、やめるときお金がかかります。かれはそれがいやでした。\n\nそこで、AIを使って新しいソフトを作りました。フォトショップやイラストレーターなど、七つのソフトです。見た目も使い方もアドビとよく似ています。ぜひむりょうで使えます。\n\nトーマスさんは「一か月で百パーセント同じになる」と言いました。でも、あとで「九十九パーセントは、何か月もかかる」と言いました。まだとても早いです。\n\nこのソフトはまだ未完成です。こわれやすいです。それに、アドビとそっくりなので、もんだいになるかもしれません。\n\nトーマスさんは言います。「ソフトはもうおわりだ。みんなでインターネットをとりもどそう」と。", "body_zh": "美国有个叫布兰登·托马斯的人。他是做软件的。Adobe的软件很贵。而且取消订阅还要花钱。他很讨厌这一点。\n\n于是他用AI做了新软件。有Photoshop、Illustrator等七款。外观和用法都和Adobe很像。而且完全免费。\n\n托马斯说“一个月就能做到100%一样”。但后来说“99%得好几个月”。现在还非常早。\n\n这个软件还没完成。容易出问题。而且和Adobe太像，可能会有法律麻烦。\n\n托马斯说：“软件已经结束了。大家一起把互联网拿回来。”", "text": "アメリカにブランドン・トーマスという人がいます。かれはソフトを作る人です。アドビのソフトが高いです。それに、やめるときお金がかかります。かれはそれがいやでした。 そこで、AIを使って新しいソフトを作りました。フォトショップやイラストレーターなど、七つのソフトです。見た目も使い方もアドビとよく似ています。ぜひむりょうで使えます。 トーマスさんは「一か月で百パーセント同じになる」と言いました。でも、あとで「九十九パーセントは、何か月もかかる」と言いました。まだとても早いです。 このソフトはまだ未完成です。こわれやすいです。それに、アドビとそっくりなので、もんだいになるかもしれません。 トーマスさんは言います。「ソフトはもうおわりだ。みんなでインターネットをとりもどそう」と。", "vocab": [{"word": "ソフト", "pos": "noun", "zh": "软件", "note": "英语software的缩写"}, {"word": "つくる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "做，制作", "note": "五段动词"}, {"word": "つかう", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使用", "note": "五段动词"}, {"word": "むりょう", "pos": "noun", "zh": "免费", "note": "無料"}, {"word": "よく似ている", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "很像", "note": "よく＋似ている"}, {"word": "お金", "pos": "noun", "zh": "钱", "note": "お金がかかる＝花钱"}, {"word": "いや", "pos": "adj", "zh": "讨厌", "note": "な形容词"}, {"word": "もんだい", "pos": "noun", "zh": "问题", "note": "问题，麻烦"}], "title_original": "“Software is over”: Bold AI developer takes aim at Adobe with open source clones", "summary_original": "Opus-built Creative Cloud alternatives are ambitious, free, and nowhere near finished.", "body_original": "If it quacks like adobe\n“Software is over”: Bold AI developer takes aim at Adobe with open source clones\nOpus-built Creative Cloud alternatives are ambitious, free, and nowhere near finished.\nKyle Orland\n–\nOct 7, 2026 5:56 pm\n|\n74\nThink that's a screen from Photoshop? Look again...\nCredit:\nArtcraft\nThink that's a screen from Photoshop? Look again...\nCredit:\nArtcraft\nText\nsettings\nStory text\nSize\nSmall\nStandard\nLarge\nWidth\n*\nStandard\nWide\nLinks\nStandard\nOrange\n* Subscribers only\nLearn more\nMinimize to nav\nFor a while, those hoping to\navoid the difficulty and expense of dealing with Adobe’s Creative Suite\nhave been able to use\nseveral free and/or open-source alternatives\nthat replicate some or all of those capabilities. Now, one developer is using AI-powered reverse engineering to mimic the look, feel, and functionality of Adobe’s well-known software with what he hopes will soon be perfect fidelity.\nArtcraft\ngot its start\nlast year\nas a “controllable AI for artists” that allows for precise post-generation editing of AI-crafted images and videos. Over the weekend, though, the brand\ndebuted its pivot\nto\na suite of seven open source apps\nrecreating the user interface and tools found in Adobe’s Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere, Lightroom, After Effects, InDesign, and Acrobat Pro.\nIn\nannouncing those new apps on Reddit\nearlier this week,\nsoftware developer Brandon Thomas\nsaid he used Anthropic’s Claude Opus 5.5 to create “clean-room replacements” for Adobe’s closed source software in Rust (with WebAssembly versions available for use in a browser). And while commenters\non Hacker News\nand\nelsewhere\nhave\ntaken pains\nto point out the new software’s many current shortcomings, Thomas make the grandiose promise that\nthe current “super early alpha” state\nwill soon lead to something just as functional as anything Adobe has ever put out.\n“We’re going to reach 100% [feature] parity within a month,” Thomas\nstated on Reddit\nof his plans to quickly squash bugs and add features with the help of community reports. Days later,\non Hacker News\n, he amended that position slightly to say that “99% parity will take a while, but I’m sure it’ll be measured in months and not years.”\nIs software over?\nThomas, who says he has about a decade of experience working on large-scale Rust projects,\nwrote on Hacker News\nthat he was inspired to create his own open source Adobe software alternatives after being “bit by the dark pattern ‘cancellation fee’ one too many times.” Development of the totally free options offered here under MIT/Apache licenses will be funded, Thomas\nwrote\n, by selling token-based access to\nthe pre-existing Artcraft visual AI model and IDE\n, which is offered as an imagery-generation option inside the apps alongside third-party models. This revenue stream will help ensure these apps aren’t “going to be some orphaned small-team project,” Thomas wrote. “We have a team building popular software for filmmakers, so supporting this is fully funded.”\nThomas is the\nlatest in a long line\nof coders using AI tools to speed up the\nlong-standing but labor-intensive practice\nof reverse engineering (i.e., replicating the functionality of a piece of software without directly copying the code itself). While that practice has\ngenerally been found legally acceptable\n, the ArtCraft apps\ncould still face legal trouble\nif their “trade dress” too closely mimics Adobe’s familiar appearance and interface.\nAfter coding exclusively with AI tools since February, Thomas\nsaid\nhe foresees a near future when everyday developers can re-create open source versions of popular paid software to “take back the internet and own tech forever.”\n“Now you can just create 1:1 functional equivalents, clean room, that are highly performant and cross-platform. Nothing is stopping you,” Thomas wrote. “We’ll replace Google Search, we’ll build our own smartphones, we’ll build better infra. We’ll remove all the ads and de-enshittify the entire tech world.”\n“Software is over,” he gloated in\nan earlier comment\n, claiming to have “one-shotted Photoshop. The whole thing.”\nKyle Orland\nSenior Gaming Editor\nKyle Orland\nSenior Gaming Editor\nKyle Orland has been the Senior Gaming Editor at Ars Technica since 2012, writing primarily about the business, tech, and culture behind video games. He has journalism and computer science degrees from University of Maryland. He once\nwrote a whole book about\nMinesweeper\n.\n74 Comments", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T01:08:45.446425", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "アメリカ", "s": 0.163, "e": 0.588, "sm": 162, "em": 587, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "に", "s": 0.6, "e": 0.762, "sm": 600, "em": 762, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "ブランドン", "s": 0.775, "e": 1.35, "sm": 775, "em": 1350, "cs": 5, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "・", "s": 1.35, "e": 1.587, "sm": 1350, "em": 1587, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "トーマス", "s": 1.587, "e": 2.062, "sm": 1587, "em": 2062, "cs": 11, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "と", "s": 2.075, "e": 2.163, "sm": 2075, "em": 2162, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "いう", "s": 2.175, "e": 2.387, "sm": 2175, "em": 2387, "cs": 16, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "人", "s": 2.4, "e": 2.637, "sm": 2400, "em": 2637, "cs": 18, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "が", "s": 2.65, "e": 2.75, "sm": 2650, "em": 2750, "cs": 19, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "い", "s": 2.763, "e": 2.875, "sm": 2762, "em": 2875, "cs": 20, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "ます", "s": 2.888, "e": 3.25, "sm": 2887, "em": 3250, "cs": 21, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "。", "s": 3.25, "e": 4.138, "sm": 3250, "em": 4137, "cs": 23, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "かれ", "s": 4.138, "e": 4.388, "sm": 4137, "em": 4387, "cs": 24, "ce": 26, "si": 1}, {"i": 13, "w": "は", "s": 4.4, "e": 4.55, "sm": 4400, "em": 4550, "cs": 26, "ce": 27, "si": 1}, {"i": 14, "w": "ソフト", "s": 4.562, "e": 4.963, "sm": 4562, "em": 4962, "cs": 27, "ce": 30, "si": 1}, {"i": 15, "w": "を", "s": 4.975, "e": 5.062, "sm": 4975, "em": 5062, "cs": 30, "ce": 31, "si": 1}, {"i": 16, "w": "作る", "s": 5.075, "e": 5.413, "sm": 5075, "em": 5412, "cs": 31, "ce": 33, "si": 1}, {"i": 17, "w": "人", "s": 5.425, "e": 5.662, "sm": 5425, "em": 5662, "cs": 33, "ce": 34, "si": 1}, {"i": 18, "w": "です", "s": 5.675, "e": 6.05, "sm": 5675, "em": 6050, "cs": 34, "ce": 36, "si": 